An interesting point.  It depends on how faithful you want to be to the
original, and how much you want to interpret it.  While the latter is one of
the great strengths of Lojban, it is essentially an exercise in
deconstruction, and depends on the translator's interpretation of the text.

It would be a good exercise for different people to come up with
translations along the lines Michael suggests.

